# Who must approve changes, by folder. GitHub reads this from .github/CODEOWNERS.
# Written by `nexus init --role …` once; never overwritten.
# Replace every @your-org/… with your real GitHub teams or usernames before relying on it.
# Order matters: for each file, the LAST matching line decides — so the catch-all comes first.

# Everything else (code): developers
*                       @your-org/developers

# Requirements: product / business analysts
/docs/requirements/     @your-org/product

# Architecture docs and ADRs: architects
/docs/arch-docs/        @your-org/architects

# Designs: product designers
/docs/designs/          @your-org/designers

# Change-request records: architects approve the record itself
/docs/change-requests/  @your-org/architects
